# Wrapper scopes for `Section68`

> Module Section68Wrappers

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraIncome as Inc
> Using SaraStatus as St
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using Section68 as Src

Generated by `cutecat_scripts/generate_dataset.py`; edits are
overwritten. Each scope below adds no rule: it declares one input
per parameter of a top-level function of the port and returns what
that function returns. CUTECat explores one entry point per run,
and a top-level function is not one until something names it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FnApplicableAmount:
  input status content Src.FilingStatus
  output result content money

declaration scope FnReduction1:
  input agi content money
  input aa content money
  output result content money

declaration scope FnReduction2:
  input itemized content money
  output result content money

declaration scope FnSuspended:
  input y content integer
  output result content boolean

declaration scope FnStatusOfFiling:
  input st content St.Status
  output result content Src.FilingStatus

```

```catala
scope FnApplicableAmount:
  definition result equals Src.applicable_amount of status

scope FnReduction1:
  definition result equals Src.reduction_1 of agi, aa

scope FnReduction2:
  definition result equals Src.reduction_2 of itemized

scope FnSuspended:
  definition result equals Src.suspended of y

scope FnStatusOfFiling:
  definition result equals Src.status_of_filing of st

```
